# The eight per-chapter PDFs are retired; the Book is the one document.
#
# These have to be here, above the catch-all, because the catch-all is what
# makes their absence invisible. `/*  /index.html  200` means nothing on this
# site 404s: a request for a file that is gone gets the 4.8 KB SPA shell at
# HTTP 200. So `curl -O legible-swarm-whitepaper.pdf` saves HTML under a .pdf
# name, Zotero imports it as a paper, and a crawler records a live URL with the
# wrong body and no redirect to follow. A 301 to the Book is the honest answer
# for all three: it is where the chapter's text actually is now.
#
# PDF to PDF on purpose. Sending a tool that asked for a PDF to an HTML chapter
# page would reproduce the same wrong-content-at-200 failure one hop along.
